cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Magic square of squares: known facts, checked in Lean"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Carlson
    given-names: Drew
repository-code: "https://github.com/drew2apps/magic-square-of-squares-lean"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.1
date-released: 2026-11-21
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 proofs of the known necessary conditions and reformulations for a 3x3 magic square of
  squares (an open problem), and kernel-checked conditions on the ratio of the edge roots: it
  avoids 484 residue classes at 34 primes, its norm is a square modulo 7, 17, 31 and 47, and one
  edge root exceeds 500 (far below published search bounds). The problem itself is not solved.
  The Lean code and the text were written with Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - magic square of squares
  - formal verification
